# Phase 3 execution log — continuation 2026-09-26T073000Z

## Goal and scope

- Continued Phase 3 Java 5.5.1 behavior parity review. Netty type/API imitation is not required; observable remoting logic remains the goal. Phase 4 remains blocked.
- Re-read both English and Traditional Chinese Phase 3 plans; did not modify either plan.

## Source finding and implementation

- Compared `NettyRemotingClient.invokeOneway` and `NettyRemotingAbstract.invokeOnewayImpl`: Java calls outbound before-hooks before `invokeOnewayImpl` marks ONEWAY, then sets ONEWAY before attempting semaphore admission.
- Rust marked the command before spawning its owned task, so the hook observed a command that Java hooks would see before the transport flag was set. Moved `mark_oneway()` to after all outbound hooks and before semaphore admission.
- Extended `p3_outbound_rpc_hook_runs_before_oneway_admission_wait` with a hook recorder asserting both calls see `is_oneway() == false`; the scripted peer still verifies both transmitted frames have ONEWAY set.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md` and `docs/compatibility/JAVA_5_5_1_COMPATIBILITY.md` to document this correspondence.

